<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατήρης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀραρίσκω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fitted out, furnished</i> with, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χλανιδίοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					110
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀσμῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					498
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δένδρεα . . καρπῶν ἀφθονίῃσι
				κατήρεα</span> cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				78
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρπυλλος] φύλλοισι κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					69
				</span></i>
			; esp. of ships, <i>furnished with oars</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶχε πλοῖον κατῆρες ἑτοῖμον</span> had a
				<i>rowing</i> boat ready, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.21
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταρσὸς κ.</span> a
				<i>well-fitted</i> oar, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1346
			</span></i>.</div>
